The Background
The scrolling background can be a little tricky to set up correctly. Basically, you need to have two
background objects moving down the screen. As soon as the bottom object goes offscreen, you
place it above the screen. You keep flipping back and forth between them, and the player doesn’t
know this is what’s happening. To create the scrolling background, follow these steps:
1. Create a new folder named Background. Locate the Star_Sky.png image from the book
assets and import it into Unity by dragging it into the Background folder you just created.
Remember that because you made a 2D project, this image automatically imports as a
sprite.
2. Select the newly imported sprite in the Project view and change its Pixels per Unit property
in the Inspector view to 50. Drag the Star_Sky sprite into the scene and ensure that it is
positioned at (0, 0, 0).
