3. Create a new script in your Background folder named ScrollBackground and drag it onto
the background sprite in the scene. Put the following code in the script:
public float speed = -2f;
public float lowerYValue = -20f;
public float upperYValue = 40;
void Update()
{
transform.Translate(0f, speed * Time.deltaTime, 0f);
if (transform.position.y <= lowerYValue)
{
transform.Translate(0f, upperYValue, 0f);
}
}
4. Duplicate the background sprite and place it at (0, 20, 0). Run the scene. You should see
the background seamlessly stream by.
